= Parsley Sauce =

Melt the @butter{25%g} in a #saucepan and stir in the @plain flour{20%g}; when it froths, stir in half the @milk{300%ml}, then beat well until it thickens. Stir in the rest of the milk and keep stirring vigorously over the heat, until the sauce is thick and smooth.

Let the sauce simmer over a very low heat for about ~{7%minutes}, checking to make sure it doesn't stick or burn. Then stir in the @?cream{4%tbsp} (if used), the @fresh parsley{3%tbsp}(chopped) and plenty of @salt and @pepper{}(freshly ground). 

= Aubergine Fritters =

Wash the @aubergine{1%medium}(about 225 g) and remove the stem. Cut the aubergine lengthwise into slices about 6 mm (1 inch) thick then season with @salt and @pepper.

Mix the @ground almonds{50%g} with the @fresh dill{1%tsp}(chopped) and some @salt and @pepper, and spread on a flat plate. Dip the aubergine slices first in @egg{1}(beaten) and then into the ground almond mixture, making sure they are well-coated with almonds on both sides.

Heat a little @olive oil{} in a #large frying pan{} then put in the aubergine slices. They will probably have to be cooked in two batches; turn on the grill so that the first batch can be kept warm. Fry the aubergine over a moderate heat for about ~{4%minutes} per side, until crisp and golden on both sides and tender inside when pierced with a knife. Drain on kitchen paper, garnish with @fresh dill{}(to garnish) and serve with the sauce.